.TH ZHEN\-RAG 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded b06c570c" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
zhen\-rag \- RAG glue between vor (cs cheatsheet API) and a local llama\-server.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zhen\-rag
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
RAG glue between vor (cs cheatsheet API) and a local llama\-server.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-k \fIN\fR
number of top\-K topics to retrieve full content for (default 5)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-tokens \fIN\fR
llama\-server max_tokens for the response (default 800)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-topic\-chars \fIN\fR
per\-topic content cap; oversized topics are truncated to fit the context window (default 10000)
.TP
.B \-q \fISTRING\fR
question (otherwise reads from stdin)
.TP
.B \-\-seed \fIN\fR
llama\-server seed; nonzero pins sampling for reproducibility (combine with \-temperature 0 for greedy determinism)
.TP
.B \-\-show\-context
print retrieved references before the answer
.TP
.B \-\-system\-prompt\-file \fISTRING\fR
path to a file containing the system prompt; '' = built\-in default; '\-' = no system message at all (probe baseline)
.TP
.B \-\-temperature \fINUM\fR
sampling temperature (0.0 = greedy) (default 0.4)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
zhen\-rag \-q 'how do I rotate the WireGuard PSK?'
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
